s mass exit does not indicate a complete withdrawal from digital assets. Capital is instead rotating toward emerging narratives and specific altcoins. New spot products tracking Hyperliquid’s HYPE token have successfully drawn approximately $72 million. Other targeted assets like XRP and Solana (SOL) are also seeing fresh inflows, capturing $22 million and $15.6 million, respectively, according to [recent flow data](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/25/hype-funds-attract-millions-as-investors-dump-bitcoin-and-ether-etfs#1).\n\nThese movements suggest that investors are becoming highly selective. They are looking past the major benchmark assets to find concentrated value in specific ecosystems. The ability to easily access these niche markets through regulated spot products is accelerating the trend of capital rotation within the digital asset sector.\n\n## Institutions pivot to HYPE and altcoin ETFs\n\nThe divergence in fund flows highlights a maturing strategy among institutional players. Investors are increasingly willing to step away from benchmark assets like Bitcoin when momentum slows, opting instead to target high-growth protocols. The sudden influx into [HYPE spot products](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/25/hype-funds-attract-millions-as-investors-dump-bitcoin-and-ether-etfs#2) issued by firms like Bitwise and 21Shares demonstrates this precise redeployment of capital."}],"path":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260525-103551/article/raw.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","usage":{"input":2342,"output":1452,"cacheRead":11239,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15033,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779705913884,"responseId":"PCgUao3mBra-jMwPj_i9kQk"}}
