so seeing fresh inflows, capturing $22 million and $15.6 million, respectively, according to [recent flow data](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/25/hype-funds-attract-millions-as-investors-dump-bitcoin-and-ether-etfs).\n 16 \n 17 These movements suggest that investors are becoming highly selective. They are looking past the major benchmark assets to find concentrated value in specific ecosystems. The ability to easily access these niche markets through regulated spot products is accelerating the trend of capital rotation within the digital asset sector.\n 18 \n 19 ## Institutions pivot to HYPE and altcoin ETFs\n 20 \n-21 The divergence in fund flows highlights a maturing strategy among institutional players. Investors are increasingly willing to step away from benchmark assets like Bitcoin when momentum slows, opting instead to target high-growth protocols. The sudden influx into [HYPE spot products](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/25/hype-funds-attract-millions-as-investors-dump-bitcoin-and-ether-etfs#2) issued by firms like Bitwise and 21Shares demonstrates this precise redeployment of capital.\n+21 The divergence in fund flows highlights a maturing strategy among institutional players. Investors are increasingly willing to step away from benchmark assets like Bitcoin when momentum slows, opting instead to target high-growth protocols. The sudden influx into [HYPE spot products](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/25/hype-funds-attract-millions-as-investors-dump-bitcoin-and-ether-etfs) issued by firms like Bitwise and 21Shares demonstrates this precise redeployment of capital.\n 22 \n 23 This structural shift indicates a profound maturation of the digital asset space. Traders must actively adapt to these new market dynamics to maintain their edge and secure profits. Recognizing the signs of capital rotation early can provide significant trading advantages over those relying on outdated strategies. The market clearly rewards participants who pay close attention to specific protocol fundamentals rather than just passively following broad trends. These targeted investments require careful analysis of network activity, active user growth, and sustainable revenue metrics to identify the most promising opportunities.\n 24 \n 25 ### The rise of Hyperliquid and HIP-3\n    ...","firstChangedLine":15},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779705928725}}
